      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raja lived deep in the forest, where he spent his days hunting and roaming. One evening, he smelled something incredible drifting from a village nearby—spices, rice, and something he couldn't name. Curious, he crept closer and saw a grandmother stirring a huge pot of biryani. The aroma made him forget all about raw meat.\n\nThe next night, Raja returned and watched her cook from behind the trees. He memorised every step: the ginger-garlic paste, the yoghurt marinade, the layering of rice and meat, the dum on low heat. When she left, he snuck into her kitchen, found leftover ingredients, and tried it himself. His first attempt was a disaster—burnt rice, raw chicken, and he accidentally ate half the onions while chopping.\n\nBut Raja kept practising. After a dozen tries, he finally made a pot of biryani that smelled just like hers. He invited the forest animals to taste it, and they couldn't believe a tiger had cooked it. From that day on, Raja became famous—not as the fiercest hunter, but as the only tiger in the world who could make perfect biryani. He still hunted, but now he preferred his meals with saffron and cardamom.\n\n9:45 PM",
